60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate A is home follow-up. It matches the readmission success, but the tariff is zero.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate B is day rehab. It needs therapy staff, who are leaving. That is a risk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Candidate D is perinatal support. Midwifery has slack, so staffing is not an issue.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Candidate C is chronic care. It is on-site, so it bills at standard rates. That is good for revenue.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Candidate B needs dedicated space. Rooms are full. Candidate D might fit better.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if A earns no tariff, is it viable? The budget is down a quarter.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, if D uses midwifery slack, it avoids the therapy staffing crisis.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, if B needs new rooms, it will fail. The booking system cannot handle it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, A is risky financially. C and D are on-site and billable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, D fits the existing midwifery flow. B would seize up the schedule.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,I am worried about A's lack of revenue. C seems more sustainable financially.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"B is too risky on staffing. D uses existing slack, which is smart.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,D is the only one that fits the staffing reality. A and B are overburdened.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,C is on-site and billable. It avoids the home visit tariff issue.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,D fits the physical space. B and A create bottlenecks in rooms and access.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for C. It is on-site and sustainable.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for D. It uses midwifery slack and avoids therapy gaps.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for D. It fits the staffing review perfectly.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,I vote for C. It generates revenue and avoids home visit costs.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for D. It fits the physical infrastructure and booking system.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
